Test fixtures (internal/metadata/anime/testdata/offline)
  The offline cache the anime engine's golden test builds from. Only the records and responses the three test
  builds read are kept, reduced to the fields the pipeline uses; internal/metadata/anime/testdata/README.md lists
  each file.

  manami-project anime-offline-database
    https://github.com/manami-project/anime-offline-database
    Open Database License 1.0 (http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/); individual contents under the
    Database Contents License 1.0 (http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1.0/).
    Kept: the 32 looked-up records, reduced to the fields the tests use (title, type, episodes, animeSeason,
    duration, synonyms, sources, relatedAnime), in cache/static/manami-aod-minified.json. This excerpt stays under
    ODbL 1.0.

  anibridge/anibridge-mappings
    https://github.com/anibridge/anibridge-mappings
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 AniBridge.
    Kept: the 27 looked-up AniList keys of mappings.json, in cache/static/anibridge-mappings.json.

  Anime-Lists/anime-lists (ScudLee)
    https://github.com/Anime-Lists/anime-lists
    The repository publishes no licence file.
    Kept: 22 <anime> records of anime-list-master.xml (ids, default TVDB season, offsets, name and episode
    mappings), in cache/static/scudlee-anime-list-master.xml.

  Fribb/anime-lists
    https://github.com/Fribb/anime-lists
    The repository publishes no licence file.
    Kept: 34 records of anime-list-full.json, three fields (anilist_id, anidb_id, themoviedb_id), in
    cache/static/fribb-anime-list-full.json.

  AniList, Kitsu, TheXEM, Sonarr SkyHook (TVDB data)
    Recorded API responses, reduced to the fields the tests use: AniList GraphQL media batches (AniList terms: no
    mirroring or hoarding; a few dozen records, for tests only), Kitsu relationships and titles (keyless public API,
    no published terms), TheXEM map/all (no published terms), and SkyHook TVDB episode numbers, dates, titles,
    overviews and airs fields (unofficial endpoint; TVDB data).

The Cardigann definitions themselves (github.com/Prowlarr/Indexers) are not part of Theatarr: they are downloaded at
run time into the data folder and never committed or shipped.
